Z||000005||Monkeyman||11-25-2001||06:46 PM||||Umm...Why come on a Fiero forum and bash a Fiero?  Not too bright.  <P>Most of us here are die hard Fiero fanatics, but some of us like other cars as well.  My 2<sup>nd</sup> choice in cars is a Toyota Supra (Mk III).<P>Want some reasons to own a Fiero?  They handle great.  A stock GT/Formula will out corner most cars that don't cost more than your house.  They're easy to modify, too.  You can spend less than $1500USD and have a truly world class handling car.  Wanna go faster in a straight line?  How about a motor upgrade?  For less than 10 grand (including a new crate ZZ4 and labor), you can out accelerate a Vette.  Here's another reason to own a Fiero.  Safety.  During the years the Fieros were produced (1984-88), the only car to beat the Fiero in NHSTA testing was the Volvo (and that's pretty much been the safest car for about forever).  <P>Feel free to join our little community, but don't you dare come over here and start bashing the cars we love.  If you can behave, I welcome you.  If you act like a child, GO AWAY! <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/patriot.gif">    <BR><B><FONT COLOR="red">Proud</FONT> <FONT COLOR="white">to be an</FONT> <FONT COLOR="blue">American</FONT>!!</B>||||reg||1
