Z||000029||Pyric||11-25-2001||11:34 PM||||You really what to know why we LOVE them?  Try standing behind a stock V6 when the driver guns the engine.  You'll hear the sound of pure power.  <P>We're not taking a Honda Civic with glass packs... we're talking a low roar you won't forget.  It's like the difference between a Harley and a weed wacker.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>But if that's not enough, look into the possible modifications you can have.  For under 15K I could have a Fiero bodied like a Ferrari or Lamborgini with a Northstar engine and a level 2 turbo kit.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"> <BR>Believe me when I say, no car within 3x that cost could touch it in speed or handling.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"> <P>As as for everyone on the Fiero side.. be nice to the kid, I doubt he meant anything by what he said, and he was probably just unaware that the Fiero had such potential. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>"Never offend people with style when you can offend them with substance." <BR>--Sam Brown||||reg||7
